Original Zero text codec: verified 2026-11-17

Linux ELF:69/69 native command/file assertions passed.
Windows PE under Wine:69/69 identical command/file assertions passed.
Each matrix includes zero-text selftest:51/51 original-Zero decoder cases.
The selftest feeds the same decoder used by make/read/verify, rather than an
alternate implementation. Cases and one-based failure identifiers are in
original tools/text.zero source.

File checks covered empty, ASCII, Unicode and exact1MiB payload round trips;
known independent FNV1a32 bytes; header/exact-length/checksum validation;
exclusive output preservation; invalid UTF-8/NUL and oversize make refusal;
partial/trailing containers, malformed headers, non-scalar UTF-8 and checksums;
no payload leakage before validation; missing/directory inputs, existing
output directories and argument errors. Read-back and EOF are enforced by make.
The Windows NUL reserved device name was excluded from ordinary file fixtures.

Windows execution used Wine, not a newly installed physical Windows machine.
FNV1a32 is an accidental-corruption checksum, not an authenticity signature.

